# No Material / Cupertino

Flutter UI in this monorepo must not depend on Material or Cupertino design APIs.

## Do not

- Import `package:flutter/material.dart` or `package:flutter/cupertino.dart`
- Use Material/Cupertino widgets or helpers (`Material`, `Scaffold`, `AppBar`, `InkWell`, `IconButton`, `Theme`, `ThemeData`, `CupertinoButton`, …)
- Pull in Material icons / typography as the visual system for product UI

## Do

- Import `package:flutter/widgets.dart` (plus `painting`, `rendering`, `services`, `scheduler` only as needed)
- Build look and interaction with primitives: `Container`, `ColoredBox`, `GestureDetector`, `MouseRegion`, `CustomPaint`, `Text`, `RichText`, etc.
- Keep colors, metrics, and typography in package-local theme types (e.g. `VscUiTheme`), not `Theme.of(context)`

```dart
// ❌ BAD
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

IconButton(icon: Icon(Icons.search), onPressed: onTap);

// ✅ GOOD
import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';

GestureDetector(
  onTap: onTap,
  child: mouseRegionWithTooltip(/* custom icon widget */),
);
```

## Exceptions

- **Theme bridge packages** whose public purpose is mapping into Flutter `ThemeData` / `Color` (e.g. `atmos_vsc_theme_flutter`) may import `material.dart` only for that bridge API — not for building widgets.
- Do not expand Material usage elsewhere “for convenience” because an exception package already imports it.
